Well, no, since I am on this list too.  But the problem probably is to figu=
re=20
out what each of us means by "objective reality" -- and "perceive," for tha=
t=20
matter. I expect xod would join in, but with yet another set of definitions=
.=20=20
Our perceptions are influenced by a range of factors that are not now=20
external to us, but also seem, at least, to be influenced by things that ar=
e=20
external to us.  What those things are in themselves we cannot, in a sense,=
=20
know, though in another sense they have to be pretty generally what they se=
em=20
to be.  If we stress the latter point then objective reality is just the=20
agreed upon reality of the community.  If we stress the former, then=20
objective reality is unknowable and thus, may not exist (the apparently=20
external factors in perception being part of our vast unconscious).  The=20
first position turns out to make life a lot easier.

